From e63db64edeb8f922bbf50d03c5ea7556407b80ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Parpart <christian@parpart.family>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:01:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] config: define the config-enum reader in a header, so every
 caller links

YAMLConfigReader::loadFromEntry() for a ConfigEnumConcept enum was a member
template declared in Config.hpp and defined in Config.cpp only. GlobalOverrides.cpp
calls it for TabBarPosition, TabBarVisibility, UiStyle and WindowControlStyle, and
so linked only while Config.cpp's object happened to keep an out-of-line copy of
those four instantiations. GCC at -O3 inlines them all and keeps none, so the
Flathub build of 0.8.0 fails to link contour with four undefined references.

The template is now defined in Config.hpp, and loadConfigEnum() and placeOf(),
which it calls, move out of Config.cpp's anonymous namespace into
ConfigEnumReader.hpp, so each translation unit instantiates what it reads.

Signed-off-by: Christian Parpart <christian@parpart.family>
